I am not getting the Move class

Can someone explain that

public class Move {

 private static Cell cell;

 public static Cell getCell() {

 return cell;

 }

}

we are not setting the value anywhere of cell

Here is how I have optimized the code

private Cell findOptimalMove(Player player, TicTacToe ticTacToe) {

 return OffensivePlacement.getOffensivePlacement()
 .place(ticTacToe, player)
 .or(() -> DefensivePlacement.getDefensivePlacement().place(ticTacToe, player))
 .or(()-> MiddlePlacement.getMiddlePlacement().place(ticTacToe,player))
 .or(()-> CornerPlacement.getCornerPlacement().place(ticTacToe,player))
 .orElseGet(() -> findFirstAvailableCell(ticTacToe));
}

Excellent content [person or link removed]!

Quick Question though - the rate-limiter client exposes the `updateKeys()` and `getKeys()` to the caller (example Profile service).

Wondering why a business domain would keep track of the key's information as it sounds internal to the Rate-limiter solution.

Caller example:

if (limiter.shouldAccept(request)) {

 limiter.onAccept(request);

} else {

 limiter.onReject(request);

}

var res = limiter.readKey(json); 

limiter.updateKey("user123", [domain removed]unt + 1);

[person or link removed], so you mean that the rule engine should have separate functions to evaluate rules based on whether the game is timed or not. Basically , something like this 

RuleEngine{

evaluateTimedGameRules(gameConfig: GameConfig)

evaluateNonTimedGameRules()

}

Let me know if this is what you meant?
